For weeks now, I’ve seen a king fisher waiting wherever I go. It reminds me of a faded memory and makes me think there's something I should be doing.
I keep a broken sword under my bed where I never have to look at it. I should've thrown it away years ago, but I can't. It meant something important, once. I guess it still does, even if I forgot about it.
I couldn't even remember why I owned a sword. It wasn't a normal thing for a park ranger to own, but I had it.
Seeing the king fisher brought old feelings to the surface. I could feel the shadows of my past inching forward to remind me of prior shames.
I failed once. That must've been how I broke the sword. I couldn't finish my quest after that, or maybe I'd already failed by the time it was broken.\
Either way, someone else finished my quest for me. I don't feel angry about it, just sad. Disappointed, I guess.
I'm sure I could fix it now. I can take the sword from under my bed and put it in its scabbard. I could get in my car and sit, waiting for the king fisher to appear again.
And I could follow it through the forest road until I came upon a dreary building whose name already waited on my lips.
Camlann.